From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] out-of-memory handled in the staging buffer, D3D9 buffer discards, constant buffers, up buffers and Create calls, and the HUD

DxvkStagingBuffer::alloc returns an undefined slice when the device is out of
memory; Direct3D 11 UpdateSubresource, UpdateTileMappings data, the
initializer uploads and the Direct3D 9 texture and buffer uploads skip the
copy and mark the device lost, and a deferred Map returns E_OUTOFMEMORY.
Direct3D 9 DiscardMapSlice, the constant buffers and the up buffer
allocator report a null slice instead of dereferencing it, the draws and
Lock return D3DERR_OUTOFVIDEOMEMORY, and CreateVertexBuffer,
CreateIndexBuffer, CreateStateBlock and CreateAdditionalSwapChainEx return
D3DERR_OUTOFVIDEOMEMORY. HUD rendering drops the frame when its buffers
cannot be created.
